## §14.7 item 2 (5a) — bare-named-`def` value carries its Fn signature.
##
## THE BUG: a bare reference to a top-level `def` used as a VALUE (not called)
## was typed as the SIGNATURELESS scalar `TYPE_FUNCTION` — no attached
## `Fn(...): R` signature. So `option_some(bare_def)` erased the payload and the
## chained `.unwrap()` narrowed to nothing callable: `g(5)` was rejected with
## QZ0200 "Cannot call 'g': not a function".
##
## THE FIX: at the NODE_IDENT site, when a bare identifier resolves to a
## top-level `def`, synthesize a real signature-carrying `Fn` ptype from the
## function registry's param + return types (mirroring the lambda /
## `Fn(...)`-annotation builder). `tc_fn_type_id(result) >= 0` then holds, the
## `option_some(...)` payload refinement attaches the concrete `Option<Fn>`,
## and the chained-`.unwrap()` narrowing (added in the same fix) recovers a
## callable. A companion `tc_elem_type_matches` recursion keeps the now-concrete
## `Option<Fn>` matching an annotated `Vec<Option<Fn>>` element.
##
## MINIMAL ON PURPOSE: two priming effects masked the pre-fix RED unless the
## reproduction is kept to exactly this one statement:
##   1. A SECOND working `Option<Fn>.unwrap()` anywhere in the module retro-
##      actively primes the golden binary's whole-module inference fixpoint and
##      masks the first failure — so `main` holds only the bare-def core case.
##   2. The pre-fix golden RED (QZ0200 "Cannot call 'g': not a function") also
##      only reproduces when this file is compiled from OUTSIDE the in-repo
##      `spec/qz/` dir (argv[0]-relative prelude/std resolution differs by
##      compile location — same file, `/tmp/` copy = RED, in-repo = masked).
## Verified pre-fix RED via: `cp this /tmp/x.qz && quartz-pre-5a-baredef-golden
## /tmp/x.qz` → QZ0200. POST-FIX it is GREEN in every location, which is what a
## forward regression lock needs. The R1 push regression (concrete
## Vec<Option<Fn>> element match) and the lambda-payload cases live in the
## companion functional smoke `option_unannotated_closure_unwrap_smoke.qz`.
## Representation-independent.
##
## Returns 0 on success; a distinct non-zero code per failed assertion.

def bare_inc(x: Int): Int = x + 1

def main(): Int
  # CORE (RED pre-fix): chained option_some(bare_def).unwrap() then call.
  g = option_some(bare_inc).unwrap()
  if g(5) != 6
    puts("FAIL[core]: g(5) = #{str_from_int(g(5))} (expected 6)")
    return 1
  end

  puts("ALL OK")
  return 0
end
